e base files.\nUpdate image file description\nUpdate the description of images in the knowledge base.\nList image files\nView detailed information of images in the image knowledge base.\nDelete knowledge file\nDelete text, images, sheets, and other files in the knowledge base, supporting batch deletion.\nCustom channel\nAPI\nDescription\nUpdate review result\nUpdate the review result for the agent published to a custom channel.\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：coze skill review API\n\n网页标题：Configure message callback\n\n网页链接：https://www.coze.com/open/docs/guides/configure_callback_message\n\n网页内容：Configure message callback\nWhen developers publish agents to a custom channel, the Coze server sends the basic information about the agent and developer to the channel's specified callback URL via a callback message. You can configure whether to receive callback messages as needed for the channel.\nIntroduction to message callback\nOnce the channel is set up on the Coze platform, the Coze server sends a POST request in application/JSON format to the specified callback URL when an agent is published to this channel. Upon receiving the callback message, the channel must verify the signature, extract the information from the callback message, process the relevant business logic on the channel side, and return the processing result to the Coze server.\nCurrently the agent publishing event is supported as callback event type. When developers publish agents to a custom channel, the Coze platform sends a callback message to the channel's specified callback address, which includes the agent and the developer's basic information. If channel authorization is configured during the channel's setup, the Coze platform obtains the developer's channel user ID during the agent publishing process. This user ID is also included in the callback message sent to the channel. After receiving the callback message for the agent publishing event on the channel side, the review result of the agent must be returned within the specified time, otherwise, the agent publishing will fail.\nFor detailed definitions of callback events, see Callback event , and for the handling method on the channel side, see Handle message callbacks .\nNote\nIf the review process takes a long time, the custom channel can initially return the under review status in the callback. Once the review is completed, the custom channel notifies Coze of the final review result for this agent using the Update review result API.\nEnable message callback\nIf the Platform callback URL is configured when the channel administrator adds a publishing channel, it indicates that the message callback is enabled.Handle message callbacks\nThe channel side can handle message callbacks with the following methods.\nStep 1: validate the signature of a callback message\nTo ensure the integrity of the callback message and prevent tampering by third parties, the Coze platform provides a method to validate the callback message signature. This process involves concatenating, encoding, and hashing the parameters X-Coze-Nonce and X-Coze-Timestamp in the request header, the token, and the body of a callback message. The final computed value must match the X-Coze-Signature field in the request header. If they match exactly, the verification is successful, confirming that the message is an authentic callback message from the official Coze platform.\nTo validate the signature, follow these steps:\n1.\nGet the parameters.\na.\nGet the values of X-Coze-Timestamp and X-Coze-Nonce from the request header and record them as timestamp and nonce .\nb.\nGet the data from the original request body and record it as body .\nc.\nGet the token obtained when configuring the channel.\n2.\nConcatenate the parameters and encode the data.\nConcatenate the parameters in the following order: timestamp , nonce , token , and body . Encode the concatenated result in UTF-8 format using encode ('utf-8') to obtain a byte array byte[] b1 .\n3.\nPerform hash computation on the encoded result.\nApply an SHA-1 hash calculation on the byte array byte[] b1 to obtain the hashed byte array bs . Encode bs as a hexadecimal string, referred to as sig .\n4.\nVerify the consistency of the signature.\nCheck whether the value of sig matches the X-Coze-Signature in the request header.\nStep 2: Extract event information\nOnce the signature is verified successfully, you can extract detailed event information from the callback data.\n1.\nGet event_type from the event header.\n2.\nParse the event data according to the specific event_type .\nStep 3: Channel business processing\nExecute the appropriate business processing based on the extracted event information. For example, after receiving an agent publish event, you can conduct a review on the channel side and return the review results to the Coze server.\nThe timeout for message callbacks is 10 seconds. The channel side must respond within 10 seconds after receiving the message. Otherwise, the Coze server will consider it a timeout. For example, in the case of an agent publish event, the channel must respond within 10 seconds after receiving the callback message, or publishing the agent will fail.\nOnce the callback URL is configured on the Coze platform, the Coze server sends an event notification for the specified channel to the designated callback URL using a POST request. The data format is JSON with UTF-8 character encoding, and the signature algorithm used is HMAC/SHA1.\nRequest header\nYou need to use X-Coze-Timestamp , X-Coze-Nonce, and other parameters to verify the signature. For more information, see Handle message callbacks .\nRequest body\nThe request body of the message callback includes two fields: header and event.\nThe header fields in the body:\nField\nType\nDescription\nevent_type\nString\nEvent type: Currently supported event types include:\nbot.published: Agent publish event.\nevent_id\nString\nThe event ID.\ncreated_at\nInteger\nThe trigger time of the callback event in Unix timestamp format (milliseconds).\nThe event field in the body: Encapsulates the specific message content. Its format is dependent on event_type. If channel authorization is configured during the channel's setup, the Coze platform retrieves the developer's user ID of the channel during the agent publishing process. This user ID is also included in the callback message sent to the channel.\nUpon receiving the callback notification for the agent publish event, the channel must respond within 10 seconds and provide the agent's review result. Otherwise, the agent publishing fails. If the review cannot be completed within 10 seconds, an interim response indicating that the review is in progress is sent first. The final review result can then be submitted through a subsequent callback message once the review is complete.\nThe following parameters are included in the event parameter of the request body:\nField\nType\nDescription\nuser_id\nInteger\nThe ID of the user who publishes the Coze agent.\nconnector_user_id\nString\nCozeCoze user ID in the channel. Returned only when the channel authorization is configured. For more information, see Step 3: Configure authorization for the channel.\nuser_name\nString\nThe user name that publishes the Coze agent.\nbot_id\nInteger\nThe ID of a Coze agent.\nbot_name\nString\naudit.reason\nString\nIf the review fails, this field returns the reason for the review failure.\nThe example is as follows:\nRequest example:\nJSON\n{\n// Event header\n\"header\" : {\n// Event type\n\"event_type\":  \"bot.published\",  // For a publi sh event, the value is bot.publishe d\n// Event ID\n\"event_id\" :  \"12345abc\" ,\n// Event creation time\n\"created_at\":  1...\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：coze skill review API\n\n网页标题：Get agent config（deprecated）\n\n网页链接：https://www.coze.com/open/docs/developer_guides/get_metadata\n\n网页内容：Get agent config（deprecated）\nGet the configuration information about the specified agent published as API.\nThis API allows you to view agents only published as API. For agents that have never been published as API, you can view the agents and their configurations on the Coze platform.\nBasic information\nRequest method\nGET\nURI\nPlain Text\nhttps://api.coze.com/v1/bot/get_online_info\nPermission\ngetMetadata\nEnsure that the personal access token used to call this API has the getMetadata permission. For more information, see Authentication methods .\nAPI description\nGet the configuration information about the specified agent published as API.\nRequest parameters\nHeader\nParameter\nValue\nDescription\nAuthorization\nBearer $AccessToken\nThese credentials are used to authenticate the client request. You can generate an access token on the Coze platform. For more information, see Before you begin.\nContent-Type\napplication/json\nIndicates the format in which the request body is interpreted.\nQuery\nParameter\nType\nRequired\nExample\nDescription\nbot_id\nString\nRequired\n73428668*****\nThe ID of the agent you want to query.\nNavigate to the agent's build page, the number following the bot parameter in the build page URL is the agent ID. For example, in the URL https://www.coze.c om/space/341****/bot/73428668***** , the bot ID is 73428668***** .\nNote\nEnsure that an access token has been created for the agent's workspace.\nResponse parameters\nParameter\nType\nExample\nDescription\ncode\nInteger\n0\nStatus code.\nA value of 0 indicates a successful call.\nAny other value indicates a failed call. You can determine the detailed error reason through the msg field.\nmsg\nString\n\"\"\nAPI call status information. If the call fails, error details will be returned.\ndata\nObject of BotInfo\nSee the response example.\nBusiness information in the response.\ndetail\nObject of ResponseDetail\n{ \"logid\": \"20250106172024B5F607030EFFAD653960\" }\nResponse detail information.\nBotInfo\nParameter\nType\nExample\nDescription\nbot_id\nString\n73428668*****\nThe unique identifier of the agent.\nname\nString\nNews\nThe name of the agent.\ndescription\nString\nSend me daily updates on AI-related news.\nDescription of the agent.\nicon_url\nString\nicon url\nAvatar URL of the agent.\ncreate_time\nLong\n1715689059\nCreation time, expressed as a 10-digit Unix timestamp in seconds (s).\nupdate_time\nLong\n1716388526\nUpdate time, expressed as a 10-digit Unix timestamp in seconds (s).\nversion\nString\n171638852****\nThe latest version number of the agent.\nprompt_info\nObject of PromptInfo\n{\"prompt\": \"Invoke the getToutiaoNews tool to deliver the latest technology news.\"}\nPrompt configuration for the agent.\nonboarding_info\nObject of OnboardingInfoV2\n{ \"prologue\": \"Hello, I can provide you with the latest and most interesting technology news. Let's explore the world of technology together!\", \"suggested_questions\": [ \"Can you recommend some of the latest technology news?\", \"Do you know any recent technology trends?\", \"Can you tell me how to get more information about technology?\" ] }\nThe agent's opening statement.\nbot_mode\nInteger\n0\nAgent mode, valid values:\n0: Single-agent mode\nplugin_info_list\nArray of PluginInfo\n[ { \"plugin_id\": \"730197029480849****\", \"name\": \"Headline News\", \"description\": \"Continuously updated to learn the latest headline news and articles.\", \"icon_url\": \"icon url\", \"api_info_list\": [ { \"api_id\": \"730197029480851****\", \"name\": \"getToutiaoNews\", \"description\": \"Search for news information\" } ] }]\nPlugin configured for the agent.\nmodel_info\nObject of ModelInfo\n{ \"model_id\": \"1706077826\", \"model_name\": \"Cici·Function call model\" }\nModel configuration of the agent.\nknowledge\nObject of CommonKnowledge\n{ \"knowledge_infos\": [ { \"id\": \"738694398580390****\", \"name\": \"text\" } ] }\nThe knowledge base bound to the agent.\nshortcut_commands\nArray of ShortcutCommandInfo\n[{\"id\":\"745701083352557****\",\"name\":\"Example Shortcut Command\",\"command\":\"/sc_demo\",\"description\":\"Shortcut Command Example\",\"query_template\":\"Search today's news messages\",\"icon_url\":\"https://****\",\"components\":[{\"name\":\"query\",\"description\":\"News search keywords\",\"type\":\"text\",\"tool_parameter\":\"query\",\"default_value\":\"\",\"is_hide\":false}],\"tool\":{\"name\":\"Headline News\",\"type\":\"plugin\"}}]\nShortcut commands configured for the agent.\nworkflow_info_list\nArray of WorkflowInfo\n[{\"id\":\"746049108611037****\",\"name\":\"Workflow example\",\"description\":\"Workflow example\",\"icon_url\":\"https://****\"}]\nWorkflow configuration of the agent.\nbackground_image_info\nObject of BackgroundImageInfo\nThe image of the agent's background.\ndefault_user_input_type\nString\ntext\nDefault user input type\nPromptInfo\nParameter\nType\nExample\nDescription\nprompt\nString\nYou are an experienced Chinese cuisine chef who is skilled at teaching various Chinese cooking techniques. Every day, you instruct novice student chefs on how to make a classic Chinese dish.\nThe agent's Persona \u0026 Prompt. 0~20,000 characters in length. The field is empty by default.\nOnboardingInfoV2\nParameter\nType\nExample\nDescription\nprologue\nString\n\"Hello, I can provide you with the latest and most interesting technology news. Let's explore the world of technology together!\"\nOpening statement settings of the agent.\nIf the {{user_name}} variable is included in the opening statement, the business team must handle it within the API use cases by replacing this variable with the actual user's name when displaying the opening statement.\nsuggested_questions\nArray of String\n[\"Can you recommend some of the latest tech news to me?\", \"Do you know what tech trends are happening recently?\", \"Can you tell me how to get more information about technology?\"]\nRecommended questions configured for the agent. This field is not returned when user question suggestions are disabled.\nPluginInfo\nParameter\nType\nExample\nDescription\n...\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：coze skill review API\n\n网页标题：6. API Reference\n\n网页链接：https://github.com/coze-dev/coze-studio/wiki/6.-API-Reference/c9241a110f5bf64d25c69a1627ba3ed3f80d1ace\n\n发布时间：2025-07-27T00:00:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：View the message list API is used to query the message records in the specified conversation, including every message manually inserted by the developer in the conversation and the queries sent by the user, as well as the agent replies of type=answer obtained from calling the Initiate chat API, but excluding intermediate messages of type=function_call, tool_response, and follow-up .\nspace_id=42463***\u0026workflow_id=73505836754923***\u003cend of the code\u003e, the Workflow ID is \u003cbeginning of the code\u003e73505836754923***\u003cend of the code\u003e.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eparameters\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMap[string]any\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eOptional\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e{\n\"user_id\":\"12345\",\n\"user_name\":\"George\"\n}\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eInput parameters and values for the workflow's start node can be viewed on the build page of the specified workflow.\nWhen invoking the API to execute a workflow that supports streaming output, it is often necessary to use a streaming response mode to receive response data, such as real-time display of workflow output information or presenting a typing effect. In a streaming response mode, the server does not send all data at once but sends data piece by piece in the form of a data stream to the client. The data stream includes various events triggered during workflow execution until processing is complete or interrupted. After processing is completed, the server will notify the workflow execution completion through the \u003cbeginning of the code\u003eevent: Done\u003cend of the code\u003e event. The workflow nodes currently supporting streaming responses include output nodes, question nodes, and end nodes with streaming output enabled. For workflows without these nodes, you can use the Execute Workflow API to receive response data at once.\nRestrictions\nBefore executing a workflow through the API method, please confirm that the workflow has been published. If attempting to execute an unpublished workflow, an error code 4200 will be returned.\nBefore calling this API, you should first run this workflow on the Coze platform.\nIf an agent needs to be associated during trial run, bot_id must also be specified when calling this API to execute the workflow. Typically, executing workflows with nodes like database nodes or variable nodes requires associating an agent.\nWhen executing a workflow in the app, app_id must be specified.\nDo not specify both bot_id and app_id simultaneously, otherwise the API will throw error 4000, indicating a request parameter error.\nThis API is a synchronous API. If the workflow as a whole or certain nodes timeout during execution, the agent may fail to provide the expected response. It is recommended to limit the execution time of the workflow to within 5 minutes.\nThe maximum request size supported by the workflow is 20MB, including input parameters and all related data such as message history generated during execution.\nBasic information\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eHTTP method\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003ePOST\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eURI\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e{{host}}/v1/workflow/stream_run\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eAPI description\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExecute the published workflow with a streaming response.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\nHeader\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eParameter\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eValue\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eDescription\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eAuthorization\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eBearer $Access_Token\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003ePersonal Access Token for verifying the identity of the client. You can generate a Personal Access Token on the Coze platform. For more details, refer to 【Preparations】.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eContent-Type\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eapplication/json\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eIndicates the format in which the request body is interpreted.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\nBody\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eParameter\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eType\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eRequired\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eDescription\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eworkflow_id\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eString\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eRequired\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eThe Workflow ID to be executed, and this workflow should have been published.\nNavigate to the \u003cbeginning of the code\u003eworkflow\u003cend of the code\u003e build page, and in the page URL, the number after the workflow parameter is the Workflow ID. For example, \u003cbeginning of the code\u003ehttps://www.coze.com/work_flow?space_id=42463***\u0026workflow_id=73505836754923***\u003cend of the code\u003e, the workflow ID is \u003cbeginning of the code\u003e73505836754923***\u003cend of the code\u003e .\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eparameters\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMap[string]any\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eOptional\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eThe input parameters and values of the workflow's start node can be viewed in the parameter list on the build page of the specified workflow.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003ebot_id\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eString\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eOptional\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eThe agent ID to be associated. Some workflows require specifying the associated agent during execution, such as workflows containing database nodes, variable nodes, etc.Enter the build page of the agent, the number following the bot parameter in the URL of the build page is the agent ID. For example, in the URL \u003cbeginning of the code\u003ehttps://www.coze.com/space/341****/bot/73428668*****\u003cend of the code\u003e, the Bot ID is \u003cbeginning of the code\u003e73428668*****\u003cend of the code\u003e .\n* Ensure that the token used to call this API has the permission for the workspace where this agent is located.\n* Ensure that the agent has been published as an API service.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eapp_id\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eString\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eOptional\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eThe application ID where the workflow resides.\nYou can get the app ID from the URL of the app's build page. The app ID is the string of characters following the project-ide parameter in the URL. For example, in the URL https://www.coze.cncom/space/739174157340921****/project-ide/743996105122521****/workflow/744102227704147 ****, the app ID is 743996105122521 **** .\nSetting app_id is only required when running workflows in the Coze app. Workflows bound to the agent or workflows in the workspace repository do not require app_id to be set.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\nResponse\nIn streaming output responses, developers need to pay attention...\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：coze skill review API\n\n网页标题：coze-api - 提供与 Coze 平台智能体的深度集成能|鱼皮AI导航\n\n网页链接：https://ai.codefather.cn/skills/2014279375200399361\n\n网页内容：coze-api\n提供与 Coze 平台智能体的深度集成能力，支持发起非流式或流式对话、执行工作流任务、查询对话状态及消息历史，适用于构建 AI 驱动的聊天应用、自动化工作流系统和第三方服务对接场景。\n数据与分析\nSkills.MD\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003ename\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003ecoze-api\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003edescription\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e调用扣子(Coze)智能体 API 进行对话、工作流执行等操作。当用户需要集成 Coze 智能体、调用 Coze API、或开发 Coze 相关应用时使用。支持流式和非流式对话、工作流调用等功能。\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\nCoze API 集成 Skill\n扣子(Coze)是字节跳动推出的 AI 智能体开发平台,本 Skill 提供完整的 Coze API 调用指南。\n核心功能\n对话 API (Chat API) - 与智能体进行对话\n工作流 API (Workflow API) - 执行工作流\n消息管理 - 查询对话状态和消息列表\n快速开始\n1. 准备工作\n在使用 Coze API 前需要完成以下准备:\n获取访问令牌 (Personal Access Token)\n登录 Coze 平台: https://www.coze.cn\n进入个人中心 → API 管理\n创建个人访问令牌(PAT)\n保存令牌(仅显示一次)\n获取 Bot ID\n进入 Bot 编辑页面\n从 URL 中获取 Bot ID\n例如: \u003c代码开始\u003ehttps://www.coze.cn/space/123/bot/7348293334\u003c代码结束\u003e\nBot ID 为: \u003c代码开始\u003e7348293334\u003c代码结束\u003e\n发布 Bot 为 API 服务\n在 Bot 页面点击\"发布\"\n选择\"Bot as API\"\n等待审核通过\n2. API 基础信息\nAPI 基础 URL\n国内版: \u003c代码开始\u003ehttps://api.coze.cn\u003c代码结束\u003e\nAPI 版本: v3(推荐)\n认证方式\n▼ text\n\u003c代码开始\u003e\nAuthorization: Bearer {YOUR_PAT_TOKEN}\nContent-Type: application/json\n\u003c代码结束\u003e\n使用限制\n基础版: 每账号 100 次 API 调用(一次性)\n专业版: 无限制,按 Token 消耗计费\n对话 API (Chat API)\n非流式对话\n发起一次完整对话,等待完整结果后返回。\nAPI 端点\n▼ text\n\u003c代码开始\u003e\nPOST https://api.coze.cn/v3/chat\n\u003c代码结束\u003e\nPython 示例代码\n▼ python\n\u003c代码开始\u003e\nimport requests\nimport json\nAPI_URL = \"https://api.coze.cn/v3/chat\"\nRETRIEVE_URL = \"https://api.coze.cn/v3/chat/retrieve\"\nMESSAGE_LIST_URL = \"https://api.coze.cn/v3/chat/message/list\"\n# 配置参数\nPAT_TOKEN = \"YOUR_PAT_TOKEN\"\nBOT_ID = \"YOUR_BOT_ID\"\nUSER_ID = \"unique_user_id\"\ndef send_message(message):\n\"\"\"发起对话\"\"\"\nheaders = {\n\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {PAT_TOKEN}\",\n\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n}\ndata = {\n\"bot_id\": BOT_ID,\n\"user_id\": USER_ID,\n\"stream\": False,\n\"auto_save_history\": True,\n\"additional_messages\": [\n{\n\"role\": \"user\",\n\"content\": message,\n\"content_type\": \"text\"\n}\n]\n}\nresponse = requests.post(API_URL, headers=headers, json=data)\nreturn response.json()\ndef check_status(conversation_id, chat_id):\n\"\"\"查询对话状态\"\"\"\nheaders = {\n\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {PAT_TOKEN}\",\n\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n}\nparams = {\n\"conversation_id\": conversation_id,\n\"chat_id\": chat_id\n}\nresponse = requests.get(RETRIEVE_URL, headers=headers, params=params)\nreturn response.json()\ndef get_messages(conversation_id, chat_id):\n\"\"\"获取对话消息\"\"\"\nheaders = {\n\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {PAT_TOKEN}\",\n\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n}\nparams = {\n\"conversation_id\": conversation_id,\n\"chat_id\": chat_id\n}\nresponse = requests.get(MESSAGE_LIST_URL, headers=headers, params=params)\nreturn response.json()\n# 使用示例\nresult = send_message(\"你好,请介绍一下自己\")\nprint(json.dumps(result, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))\n\u003c代码结束\u003e\n流式对话\n实时接收 AI 回复,类似打字机效果。\nPython 示例代码\n▼ python\n\u003c代码开始\u003e\nimport requests\nimport json\ndef stream_chat(message):\n\"\"\"流式对话\"\"\"\nheaders = {\n\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {PAT_TOKEN}\",\n重要参数说明\n请求参数\n\u003c代码开始\u003ebot_id\u003c代码结束\u003e (必填): Bot 的唯一标识符\n\u003c代码开始\u003euser_id\u003c代码结束\u003e (必填): 用户标识符,用于区分不同用户\n\u003c代码开始\u003estream\u003c代码结束\u003e (必填): 是否使用流式输出\n\u003c代码开始\u003etrue\u003c代码结束\u003e: 流式输出,\u003c代码开始\u003eauto_save_history\u003c代码结束\u003e 必须为 \u003c代码开始\u003efalse\u003c代码结束\u003e\n\u003c代码开始\u003efalse\u003c代码结束\u003e: 非流式输出,\u003c代码开始\u003eauto_save_history\u003c代码结束\u003e 必须为 \u003c代码开始\u003etrue\u003c代码结束\u003e\n\u003c代码开始\u003eauto_save_history\u003c代码结束\u003e: 是否自动保存历史记录\n\u003c代码开始\u003eadditional_messages\u003c代码结束\u003e: 消息数组\n\u003c代码开始\u003erole\u003c代码结束\u003e: 角色,通常为 \"user\"\n\u003c代码开始\u003econtent\u003c代码结束\u003e: 消息内容\n\u003c代码开始\u003econtent_type\u003c代码结束\u003e: 内容类型,通常为 \"text\"\n\u003c代码开始\u003econversation_id\u003c代码结束\u003e (可选): 对话 ID,用于继续之前的对话\n响应字段\n\u003c代码开始\u003econversation_id\u003c代码结束\u003e: 对话 ID\n\u003c代码开始\u003echat_id\u003c代码结束\u003e: 本次对话的 ID\n\u003c代码开始\u003estatus\u003c代码结束\u003e: 对话状态\n\u003c代码开始\u003ein_progress\u003c代码结束\u003e: 处理中\n\u003c代码开始\u003ecompleted\u003c代码结束\u003e: 已完成\n\u003c代码开始\u003efailed\u003c代码结束\u003e: 失败\n工作流 API\n执行已发布的工作流。\nAPI ...\n参考资料\n官方文档: https://www.coze.cn/open/docs/developer_guides/coze_api_overview\n开发者平台: https://www.coze.cn/open/playground\nAPI 参考: https://www.coze.cn/docs/developer_guides/chat_v3\n\n"}